<!-- ═══════════════════════ FAQ ═══════════════════════ -->
<section class="relative z-[1] py-20 border-b border-border">
  <div class="max-w-[1240px] mx-auto px-8 max-md:px-5">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-[1fr_2fr] max-[820px]:grid-cols-1 gap-12 max-[820px]:gap-8">
      <div>
        <span class="pr-eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span>faq</span>
        <h2 class="font-display text-[clamp(24px,3vw,32px)] font-semibold -tracking-[0.022em] leading-[1.15] mt-4">Frequently asked.</h2>
        <p class="text-[14px] text-muted-foreground mt-3 max-w-[40ch]">Didn't find your answer?</p>
        <a href="mailto:hi@backlex.com" class="pr-btn pr-btn-ghost mt-3 inline-flex">hi@backlex.com</a>
      </div>
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-2.5">
        <details class="faq glass overflow-hidden">
          <summary class="px-5 py-4 flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="text-[14.5px] font-medium">Will you charge my card on the free tier?</span>
            <svg class="chev ml-auto text-muted-foreground" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
          </summary>
          <div class="px-5 pb-4 text-[13px] text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">No. No card on free, and no auto-buy on any plan. When you reach a limit we throttle that dimension and tell you — upgrade, add a pack, or export and self-host.</div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq glass overflow-hidden">
          <summary class="px-5 py-4 flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="text-[14.5px] font-medium">What if infrastructure prices change?</span>
            <svg class="chev ml-auto text-muted-foreground" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
          </summary>
          <div class="px-5 pb-4 text-[13px] text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">On annual — your price is locked until renewal. On monthly — we email 30 days ahead; you automatically benefit from any cuts.</div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq glass overflow-hidden">
          <summary class="px-5 py-4 flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="text-[14.5px] font-medium">My workload needs full Postgres. What are my options?</span>
            <svg class="chev ml-auto text-muted-foreground" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
          </summary>
          <div class="px-5 pb-4 text-[13px] text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">The managed cloud database is capped at 10&nbsp;GB. Keep large blobs in object storage (separately billed, effectively uncapped). If you need full Postgres, the open-source backlex runs on any Postgres — self-host it with one-click export from Cloud.</div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq glass overflow-hidden">
          <summary class="px-5 py-4 flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="text-[14.5px] font-medium">What if I want to take my data out?</span>
            <svg class="chev ml-auto text-muted-foreground" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
          </summary>
          <div class="px-5 pb-4 text-[13px] text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">Every plan can export the project as a portable SQL dump — schema and data — once a day. Uploaded files stay in your object storage and aren't folded into the dump yet. It is the same Apache-2.0 backlex, so the dump restores on your own infrastructure in minutes. No contract lock-in.</div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq glass overflow-hidden">
          <summary class="px-5 py-4 flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="text-[14.5px] font-medium">Can I require data to stay in a specific region?</span>
            <svg class="chev ml-auto text-muted-foreground" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
          </summary>
          <div class="px-5 pb-4 text-[13px] text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">Yes, on every plan — you choose residency when you create the organization, and it is fixed from then on. <strong class="text-foreground font-medium">European Union</strong> creates the database and the bucket in Cloudflare's EU jurisdiction, and read replicas stay in the EU too. <strong class="text-foreground font-medium">Global</strong> lets Cloudflare place the primary across our eight regions for the lowest latency. A DPA is available.</div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq glass overflow-hidden">
          <summary class="px-5 py-4 flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="text-[14.5px] font-medium">I already self-host. Why switch to Cloud?</span>
            <svg class="chev ml-auto text-muted-foreground" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
          </summary>
          <div class="px-5 pb-4 text-[13px] text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">Often, don't. If self-host works and your team enjoys uptime, migrations, and backups — stay. Cloud is for solo devs and scale-ups who don't have that role.</div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

